WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:16.000
You apply to the council for a place at a state school, even if you come from abroad. You rank schools by preference and can appeal if you do not get a place. Most children start «reception» in the September after they turn 4.

2
00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:22.000
Each council publishes the term and holiday dates.

3
00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:38.000
Children may only miss school if they are too ill or with the school's prior permission. Going on holiday in term time can mean a fine of £80 per parent (£160 if not paid within 21 days).

4
00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:54.000
School meals: free in reception, year 1 and year 2 at state schools in England, and from the 2026-2027 school year also if you get Universal Credit. Uniform: from September 2026, at most 3 branded items (4 at secondary if one is a tie).

5
00:00:54.000 --> 00:01:01.200
Now do the lesson exercises. If you are unsure, watch this video again.
